cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenEMT in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenEMT: an agent-native electromagnetic transient simulator for electric power systems"
abstract: >-
  OpenEMT is an electromagnetic transient (EMT) and power-flow simulator for
  AC, DC and hybrid AC/DC power systems. One pure, deterministic solver core
  is addressable through three coequal frontends: a drag-and-drop schematic
  canvas that runs entirely in a web browser from a single self-contained file
  with no installation, a command-line interface for scripts and continuous
  integration, and a Model Context Protocol server whose tool schemas are
  generated from the block catalogue, so that a software agent can enumerate
  the available physics, build a circuit, solve it, and query results by
  stable block identifier. Circuits are stored as plain-text JSON. Block
  models are averaged and simplified for concept validation rather than
  certified engineering analysis; each is checked against an analytical or
  independent-solver reference, and the known limitations are published
  alongside the code.
type: software
